WEBVTT

00:02.970 --> 00:02.980
How you doin'?

00:02.980 --> 00:04.260
KANRIN TAVERN
COME ON IN
- How you doin'?

00:04.260 --> 00:05.230
KANRIN TAVERN
COME ON IN

00:05.230 --> 00:08.710
Did you hear?The list of our members' names?

00:09.560 --> 00:13.410
We were told to submit it again this year.

00:15.470 --> 00:18.570
They're gonna slap us all
onto the villain list.

00:18.920 --> 00:23.380
Just 'cause we yakuza do the
whole chivalrous gangster thing,

00:23.380 --> 00:25.460
we get treated like rotten villains.

00:25.460 --> 00:27.620
That's how the authorities do things.

00:28.960 --> 00:30.880
Why d'you look so calm?!

00:30.880 --> 00:32.420
Ain't you listenin', Rojiya?!

00:32.420 --> 00:33.810
Tetsu, sir...

00:36.090 --> 00:39.740
"Treated like villains." Sure, why not?

00:39.740 --> 00:40.810
Sir?

00:42.490 --> 00:47.680
The way a man lives doesn't change
because of policy, or the times.

00:47.690 --> 00:48.000
DRUNK DRIVING!!

00:48.000 --> 00:53.150
DRUNK DRIVING!!
- Even if you have to go up against All Might,
you still stick to your guns.

00:53.150 --> 00:53.830
DRUNK DRIVING!!

00:53.830 --> 00:56.740
DRUNK DRIVING!!
- You said it, Rojiya!

00:56.740 --> 00:59.020
DRUNK DRIVING!!
- Drink! Drink some more!

00:59.020 --> 00:59.650
DRUNK DRIVING!!
- Yeah.

00:59.650 --> 00:59.660
DRUNK DRIVING!!

01:00.170 --> 01:01.970
The Abegawa Tenchu Gang.

01:01.970 --> 01:06.630
A villain group that was a typical
yakuza gang in the pre-Quirk days.

01:06.670 --> 01:08.360
SEVERAL MONTHS AGO

01:08.360 --> 01:09.500
SEVERAL MONTHS AGO
- Its lieutenants all possess
overwhelming Quirks,

01:09.500 --> 01:10.880
Its lieutenants all possess
overwhelming Quirks,

01:10.880 --> 01:12.760
ABEGAWA TENCHU- Its lieutenants all possess
overwhelming Quirks,

01:12.760 --> 01:12.940
ABEGAWA TENCHU
NARUHATA HQ- Its lieutenants all possess
overwhelming Quirks,

01:12.940 --> 01:16.470
ABEGAWA TENCHU
NARUHATA HQ- but it's not the strength of their Quirks
that makes them truly dangerous.

01:16.470 --> 01:17.070
ABEGAWA TENCHU- but it's not the strength of their Quirks
that makes them truly dangerous.

01:17.070 --> 01:17.380
ABEGAWA TENCHU

01:23.020 --> 01:25.400
What gang sent you?!

01:25.400 --> 01:26.190
Huh?!

01:26.190 --> 01:28.230
It's how quickly and violently
they leap into battle.

01:28.230 --> 01:29.020
- It's how quickly and violently
they leap into battle.
- Nice try, stupid!

01:29.020 --> 01:29.560
HONOR AND HUMANITYTETSU THE TANK
- It's how quickly and violently
they leap into battle.
- Nice try, stupid!

01:29.560 --> 01:29.810
TETSU THE TANK
- It's how quickly and violently
they leap into battle.
- Nice try, stupid!

01:29.810 --> 01:30.030
- It's how quickly and violently
they leap into battle.
- Nice try, stupid!

01:30.030 --> 01:31.060
It's how quickly and violently
they leap into battle.

01:31.520 --> 01:31.530
SOJI THE HAMMER

01:31.530 --> 01:32.230
SOJI THE HAMMER
- Take this!

01:32.230 --> 01:34.010
Take this!

01:37.240 --> 01:38.110
HARUHISA THE BARE-HANDED

01:39.570 --> 01:40.780
ROJIYA THE MANHOLE

01:40.980 --> 01:41.970
However!

01:46.320 --> 01:47.000
Wha?!

01:48.590 --> 01:49.570
I...

01:49.570 --> 01:51.010
Can't...

01:51.010 --> 01:52.380
Can't move!

01:53.450 --> 01:57.180
For whatever reason,
all four suddenly freeze up!

01:59.180 --> 02:02.650
He uses that instant to cut them all down!

02:04.570 --> 02:05.560
Sir?!

02:05.560 --> 02:06.730
Boss!

02:07.560 --> 02:09.910
Wh-Who the hell're you?!

02:14.920 --> 02:18.200
I am Judgment. I am Stendhal.

02:25.930 --> 02:29.020
Hi, Mr. Judgment.

02:29.020 --> 02:29.960
Wrong.

02:29.960 --> 02:34.520
Yes, I know, it's "Stendhal."

02:34.520 --> 02:35.970
That's wrong too.

02:37.480 --> 02:42.280
He—Stendhal—is a superhuman being.

02:42.280 --> 02:44.620
The red of life and the black of death....

02:44.620 --> 02:48.180
The persona of judgment who
carves out the space between.

02:48.580 --> 02:53.540
With my mask off, I'm no more than an
ordinary man who serves the heroic ideal.

02:53.540 --> 02:55.720
I'd prefer the two be kept separate.

02:55.720 --> 02:58.330
Oh wow, what a pain.

02:58.330 --> 03:02.910
Okay, then, Mr. Ordinary Man. I need
to retrieve those blood samples.

03:04.050 --> 03:06.580
I bet these came in handy.

03:06.580 --> 03:11.010
Those yakuza guys really take
advantage of employee benefits.

03:11.010 --> 03:13.090
But medical check-ups can prove fatal.

03:13.470 --> 03:17.440
So, I helped you take out some bad guys.

03:17.440 --> 03:20.520
You think maybe I could
name your next target.

03:20.520 --> 03:22.200
Don't push your luck, villain.

03:22.200 --> 03:24.640
Someday Stendhal will judge you too.

03:25.300 --> 03:30.960
But until then, vermin who feed
on other vermin have their value.

03:31.670 --> 03:32.530
Right, right.

03:33.020 --> 03:35.790
Fight fire with fire, or whatever.

03:35.790 --> 03:38.020
Okay, cool. Let's do it that way.

03:38.940 --> 03:46.910
After all, the town of Naruhata
has plenty of bad villains.

05:18.290 --> 05:19.420
VILLAIN

05:19.420 --> 05:24.340
VILLAIN
A CHARACTER IN A STORY OR PLAY WHO OPPOSES THE HERO;
A DELIBERATE SCOUNDREL OR CRIMINAL;
ONE BLAMED FOR A PARTICULAR EVIL OR DIFFICULTY

05:24.340 --> 05:25.340
VILLAIN
A CHARACTER IN A STORY OR PLAY WHO OPPOSES THE HERO;
A DELIBERATE SCOUNDREL OR CRIMINAL;
ONE BLAMED FOR A PARTICULAR EVIL OR DIFFICULTYCROSSING LINES

05:25.340 --> 05:26.380
CROSSING LINES

05:30.510 --> 05:30.600
MOYURU TOCHI

05:30.600 --> 05:32.970
MOYURU TOCHI
- Hey. You're lookin' well.

05:32.970 --> 05:33.270
Hey. You're lookin' well.

05:33.270 --> 05:33.370
SOGA KUGIZAKI
- Hey. You're lookin' well.

05:33.370 --> 05:34.980
SOGA KUGIZAKI

05:35.770 --> 05:35.850
RAPT TOKAGE

05:35.850 --> 05:37.050
RAPT TOKAGE
- 'Sup?

05:37.050 --> 05:37.940
RAPT TOKAGE

05:39.840 --> 05:42.890
Here, a drink, and a copy
of Jump I'm done reading.

05:43.620 --> 05:45.740
That's your idea of a pick-me-up?

05:45.740 --> 05:47.810
Well, it's better than nothing.

05:47.810 --> 05:50.820
Never mind that, Moyu. You got a light?

05:50.820 --> 05:53.290
They confiscated my lighter.

05:53.290 --> 05:55.050
Sure thing, man.

05:57.530 --> 06:00.210
No smoking in the hospital, Rapt!

06:00.210 --> 06:01.510
Shit!

06:02.580 --> 06:05.710
They said they'll discharge me once
I see my exam results this weekend.

06:05.710 --> 06:07.840
That's sooner than I thought.

06:07.840 --> 06:11.370
I mean, you got all busted up
when you slammed into that wall.

06:11.980 --> 06:14.730
I'm a lizard. Can't keep me down for long.

06:15.330 --> 06:17.170
Thank that Quirk of yours.

06:17.440 --> 06:20.930
Shouldn't you also thank
that drug we were on?

06:20.930 --> 06:25.370
Yeah, Trigger. I'm not so sure.

06:25.370 --> 06:28.080
Maybe that's the reason
I didn't die instantly,

06:28.080 --> 06:30.550
but that stuff's why I nearly
got killed in the first place.

06:30.550 --> 06:32.830
Can't say I feel too grateful.

06:34.530 --> 06:38.060
Well, getting to fly was kinda cool.

06:38.060 --> 06:40.130
Yeah, that was sweet.

06:40.130 --> 06:44.550
I thought about it, and upping my
firepower didn't really mean much.

06:44.550 --> 06:45.620
Huh?

06:45.840 --> 06:48.630
It was awesome, though. Like Endeavor.

06:48.630 --> 06:51.010
Don't compare me to him!

06:53.240 --> 06:57.550
Hey, Rapt. You think you'd like to fly again?

06:57.830 --> 07:00.030
Huh? No way.

07:00.290 --> 07:04.910
I flew, got thrown around, fell,
and landed in the hospital.

07:04.910 --> 07:06.870
If that didn't teach me, I'm an idiot.

07:06.870 --> 07:08.100
I'll say.

07:08.570 --> 07:12.210
Oh hey, this hospital's got
some hot nurses, yeah?

07:12.570 --> 07:14.320
Land yourself in here too!

07:14.320 --> 07:16.140
Maybe I will!

07:21.850 --> 07:23.830
Hi, Soga.

07:24.300 --> 07:26.540
Oh? Where are your friends?

07:26.840 --> 07:29.060
This don't involve them.

07:29.060 --> 07:32.700
Aw, but all three of you need to know this.

07:32.700 --> 07:34.760
It's been in the news, you know.

07:34.760 --> 07:34.770
BREAKING: BLOODBATH AT CRIMINAL GANG'S HEADQUARTERS
- It's been in the news, you know.

07:34.770 --> 07:38.740
BREAKING: BLOODBATH AT CRIMINAL GANG'S HEADQUARTERS
- "Bloodbath at Criminal Gang's
Headquarters in Danto Ward."

07:38.740 --> 07:41.430
BREAKING: BLOODBATH AT CRIMINAL GANG'S HEADQUARTERS
- They said "It looked like a
scene straight out of hell."

07:41.430 --> 07:41.440
BREAKING: BLOODBATH AT CRIMINAL GANG'S HEADQUARTERS
- You guys are being targeted by a scary
murderer who wiped out a yakuza gang!

07:41.440 --> 07:47.140
You guys are being targeted by a scary
murderer who wiped out a yakuza gang!

07:47.140 --> 07:49.630
You've got to join forces and fight back!

07:49.630 --> 07:51.520
Drop the act. It's pissing me off.

07:52.150 --> 07:56.600
What I'm sayin' is, I'll take
on this murderer alone!

07:56.600 --> 08:00.530
Cool, cool. You don't want
to drag your buds into this.

08:00.530 --> 08:03.880
Well, being highly motivated's a good thing.

08:03.880 --> 08:07.830
And I guess the whole "fighting to
protect what's important" thing works.

08:08.420 --> 08:09.830
You can stop now.

08:13.350 --> 08:15.430
That's enough playing around.

08:15.430 --> 08:17.520
I'll slay him and move on to the next.

08:17.520 --> 08:20.710
So, yeah, he's primed to kill too.

08:20.710 --> 08:25.900
Okay, Soga. If you lose,
Rapt and Moyuru get offed as well.

08:25.900 --> 08:28.220
Fight like your life depends on it.

08:28.220 --> 08:29.360
Ciao.

08:33.990 --> 08:37.450
Things ain't gonna go the way you guys want.

08:38.000 --> 08:40.290
Come get some, you masked freak.

08:40.290 --> 08:43.990
I don't need drugs to deal with you.

08:44.390 --> 08:46.380
These'll do just fine!

08:48.900 --> 08:50.550
Oh yeah?

08:50.550 --> 08:51.810
That's boring.

08:57.790 --> 09:01.710
So boring, I'm gonna juice things up.

09:13.910 --> 09:16.590
Go for broke, you two.

09:17.180 --> 09:19.570
Yeah, she's like the rest.

09:20.480 --> 09:22.780
With that big grin on her face.

09:23.140 --> 09:25.980
Soga hurt Minoru!

09:25.980 --> 09:27.160
That's right.

09:27.160 --> 09:29.870
Mommy said I'm not allowed to play with you.

09:29.870 --> 09:31.540
It's always the same!

09:31.540 --> 09:33.870
You get into fights day after day.

09:33.870 --> 09:36.100
They have a word for people
like you: "villain."

09:36.100 --> 09:39.280
People who discriminate piss me off.

09:39.280 --> 09:41.450
Don't judge me by my appearance!

09:41.450 --> 09:43.310
These people are always...

09:43.930 --> 09:45.360
I'm sorry.

09:45.360 --> 09:47.630
...grinning while they...

09:48.570 --> 09:51.830
turn me... turn me...

10:00.470 --> 10:03.430
into a monster!

10:07.380 --> 10:10.080
What's that sound? A scream?

10:14.930 --> 10:16.910
You've shown your true colors.

10:16.910 --> 10:18.640
Die, villain.

10:24.040 --> 10:25.810
Stop right there!

10:25.810 --> 10:28.870
I'm the guy who heard a cry of grief...

10:28.870 --> 10:30.260
The Crawler!

10:32.350 --> 10:34.440
Wait, what? Huh?

10:34.760 --> 10:36.410
Mr. Stendhal?!

10:37.680 --> 10:39.820
Th-Those spikes...

10:40.160 --> 10:42.200
He's the Legendary Alum.

10:42.770 --> 10:44.810
Soga Kugizaki!

10:46.050 --> 10:47.740
Kugizaki...

10:48.440 --> 10:49.930
Soga?!

10:51.060 --> 10:52.660
He used Trigger again.

10:53.340 --> 10:56.840
Stand aside, Crawler.
I'll fell that villain.

10:56.840 --> 10:58.440
"Fell"?

10:58.440 --> 11:01.810
I mean, sure, this guy is bad news.

11:01.810 --> 11:04.270
That is, he practically is a villain,

11:04.270 --> 11:07.550
but you two should really try
to talk things—

11:23.140 --> 11:27.460
He's actually... attempting to kill him!

11:28.910 --> 11:29.950
Not on my watch!

11:43.670 --> 11:46.330
Ow, ow, ow! That's stabby!

11:46.330 --> 11:47.880
Why don't you retract these spikes?!

11:52.560 --> 11:54.730
Don't interfere, Crawler!

11:55.280 --> 11:58.060
There's no value in saving that man.

11:58.060 --> 12:01.240
Creeping through the darkness to his
death would be a fitting end for him.

12:01.240 --> 12:04.460
Well, you're probably right...

12:04.460 --> 12:06.140
But still!

12:10.450 --> 12:13.460
Wh-Whadda you think you're doing?

12:13.460 --> 12:17.490
Trying to get away, duh!
Like there's any other choice!

12:17.490 --> 12:20.010
Got to get to a crowded main street!

12:21.690 --> 12:23.250
Well, then...

12:23.250 --> 12:26.220
Even if an action is born of goodness,

12:26.220 --> 12:30.790
it would seem those who side
with evil... are evil.

12:37.270 --> 12:40.610
STOP

12:43.230 --> 12:46.320
I can't... move..

12:47.700 --> 12:50.540
Judgment: Stendhal. Quirk: Bloodcurdle.

12:50.540 --> 12:51.840
QUIRK: BLOODCURDLE
- Judgment: Stendhal. Quirk: Bloodcurdle.

12:51.840 --> 12:55.830
QUIRK: BLOODCURDLE
- By licking someone's blood,
he can immobilize them.

12:55.830 --> 12:56.180
By licking someone's blood,
he can immobilize them.

12:57.620 --> 12:59.460
You're through, villains.

12:59.460 --> 13:03.180
Heaven's judgment is going
to put you six feet under.

13:03.650 --> 13:06.630
No one will save you wrongdoers.

13:06.630 --> 13:08.330
No one will worry about you.

13:08.790 --> 13:11.400
No one will take the slightest notice.

13:11.400 --> 13:12.890
Not now, not here.

13:15.390 --> 13:17.360
Nope, think again!

13:24.600 --> 13:26.250
I'm here!

13:41.690 --> 13:43.380
I-It's you...

13:43.380 --> 13:45.210
M-Master!

13:46.220 --> 13:50.090
You there, your name's Stendhal?

13:51.080 --> 13:53.620
I hear you helped out my boy there.

13:58.090 --> 14:02.540
The Naruhata Vigilante, Knuckleduster.

14:05.280 --> 14:07.400
I do not wish to fight you.

14:08.890 --> 14:12.150
We follow the path of righteousness
in this twisted society.

14:12.150 --> 14:14.610
Our goal is the same, you and—

14:14.610 --> 14:16.290
No way is it the same.

14:17.330 --> 14:19.960
I'm a badass hero of justice.

14:20.300 --> 14:23.690
You're some crazy slasher.

14:25.300 --> 14:29.500
So, I can't get you to
understand me. Too bad.

14:29.500 --> 14:33.560
Don't you mean, too bad you lost
your chance for a surprise attack?

14:33.560 --> 14:37.680
It's obvious you've been sizing me up.

14:38.100 --> 14:42.280
It's easy to say, "One more step,
and I can hit him."

14:42.940 --> 14:47.110
But if I'm too far away, your first swing
will miss, leaving you vulnerable.

14:47.650 --> 14:52.700
And if I'm too close, you're within
my range. It's tricky, huh?

14:53.080 --> 14:56.080
But I'm a nice guy.

14:56.670 --> 14:59.290
I'll simplify things!

15:01.720 --> 15:02.950
A wire?

15:03.470 --> 15:06.370
If you give up and leave now, great.

15:06.730 --> 15:11.560
The moment you cross that line,

15:12.900 --> 15:14.840
that's when you get to taste these!

15:15.580 --> 15:19.730
Ah, so that's what your range is.

15:20.570 --> 15:22.320
It's worth pointing out,

15:23.490 --> 15:24.940
you're an iron wall.

15:25.960 --> 15:29.200
If you focus all your
attention on countering,

15:29.500 --> 15:33.020
it completely offsets the
advantage my weapon gives me.

15:33.670 --> 15:36.300
My only choice is to fall back!

15:37.840 --> 15:40.750
But I will cross it!

15:41.170 --> 15:44.460
My running ability is far above average.

15:44.830 --> 15:47.670
He can't possibly nail the timing of
my charge when he's never seen it!

15:48.030 --> 15:50.120
Besides, a hero...

15:50.630 --> 15:53.110
A hero is an exceptional being!

15:53.590 --> 15:56.310
He stands apart from
common sense. Beyond it.

15:56.530 --> 15:58.810
He steps over the line!

16:12.120 --> 16:15.120
Uh, hey... M-Master?

16:15.410 --> 16:18.290
You just said, "Don't cross this line."

16:19.090 --> 16:22.040
Hey, doesn't mean I can't cross it.

16:27.210 --> 16:30.670
Hmph. He puts on a mask
and becomes someone else.

16:30.670 --> 16:32.930
You run into guys like that now and then.

16:33.620 --> 16:38.290
They put on a mask or a disguise, and they're
convinced they're no longer their usual selves.

16:38.290 --> 16:41.230
They think they're some unbeatable superman.

16:41.550 --> 16:43.640
Guys like that are trouble,

16:43.640 --> 16:47.690
because they ignore social mores,
and their own safety when they come at you.

16:48.100 --> 16:51.120
But they're also fragile
when you come at them.

16:52.720 --> 16:55.840
"I'm just a flesh-and-blood
human too, in the end."

16:56.520 --> 17:02.490
Someone who's forgotten that ultimately
doesn't have much resolve.

17:04.790 --> 17:06.400
I see.

17:07.600 --> 17:09.370
I understand now.

17:33.810 --> 17:39.490
Even more wicked than villains are
those without resolve, who pretend.

17:42.910 --> 17:44.640
Sham heroes.

17:49.020 --> 17:50.260
Master!

17:50.490 --> 17:54.740
Yes, yes. Ahh, it's so true!

17:54.740 --> 17:57.110
I have been enlightened!

17:57.720 --> 18:00.670
I appreciate you showing me the way!

18:13.720 --> 18:15.190
Ow!

18:15.640 --> 18:18.150
Koichi! I heard you got hurt?!

18:18.480 --> 18:19.030
Are you all right?!

18:19.030 --> 18:19.610
- Are you all right?!
- Ow! The disinfectant stings!

18:19.610 --> 18:21.680
Ow! The disinfectant stings!

18:21.680 --> 18:24.590
It's a minor wound, didn't cut his tendon.

18:24.590 --> 18:26.830
You go see to him, girl.

18:26.830 --> 18:28.120
"Him"?

18:43.040 --> 18:45.250
Are you okay, Soga?

18:45.950 --> 18:49.860
I guess there're some scary
people in this world, huh?

18:49.860 --> 18:52.410
I'm just glad we both
got through that alive.

18:52.410 --> 18:53.890
Ow, ow!

18:53.890 --> 18:54.580
Feh!

18:55.070 --> 18:57.170
What's "feh" supposed to mean?

18:57.170 --> 18:58.510
Didn't I save you?

18:58.510 --> 19:00.030
Why're you saying that to me?

19:00.310 --> 19:03.310
Hey, what the hell's his deal?

19:03.310 --> 19:06.390
He nearly got killed,
and now he's all smiles.

19:06.390 --> 19:08.270
Is he nuts or somethin'?

19:11.310 --> 19:13.240
He's not nuts.

19:13.800 --> 19:15.130
He's an idiot!

19:20.730 --> 19:22.460
I see how it is.

19:36.030 --> 19:40.780
Power. Speed. Armaments. Tactics.

19:41.640 --> 19:45.750
Right now there are...
too many things I lack.

19:46.830 --> 19:48.980
What I lack most of all is...

19:51.030 --> 19:54.100
Yes, it's resolve!

19:56.570 --> 20:02.370
In my own opinion, I think one's work
and life should both be entertaining.

20:02.370 --> 20:06.510
And I have to say, your "resolve" might
be the most entertaining thing ever.

20:06.510 --> 20:07.140
Shut up!

20:35.380 --> 20:38.100
This will do.

20:38.100 --> 20:40.840
I have no mask anymore.

20:43.330 --> 20:45.420
My mask of vanity is broken.

20:45.870 --> 20:48.110
I discard my false face,

20:48.590 --> 20:52.440
and this time I behold the truth
of this world with uncovered eyes.

20:53.810 --> 20:58.380
No falsehood, no truth,
and no limits to exceed.

21:01.320 --> 21:06.100
Everything is right here,
blending together into chaos.

21:08.910 --> 21:13.010
There he goes again, talking
to himself all cryptic.

21:13.010 --> 21:14.590
What a narcissist.

21:14.880 --> 21:18.010
Not that I mind, though.

21:18.010 --> 21:19.660
It's entertaining.

21:21.280 --> 21:23.480
I am a faceless ideology.

21:26.040 --> 21:29.040
Action without existence.

21:30.070 --> 21:32.490
A color that dyes the world.

21:34.560 --> 21:39.390
The blood I shed, the blood I bleed,
is proof of its importance.

21:40.250 --> 21:44.180
Behind me, a path remains.

21:48.830 --> 21:52.730
Indelible bloodstains that show the way!

23:25.990 --> 23:30.280
To protect themselves, people formed
groups and fought outsiders.

23:30.280 --> 23:32.700
It was supposed to be about justice.

23:33.160 --> 23:35.020
Next time, "Makoto/Truth."

23:35.380 --> 23:39.680
From a different point of view, those groups
are merely powerful legalized violence.
